# Password Security Analysis & Policy Design

## Objective
Analyze password weaknesses (strength and reuse), implement secure password handling (hashing, salting, validation), and define a strong password policy.

> All passwords used are synthetic sample data. No real credentials are used.

## What this project covers
1. Loading sample password data
2. Strength and reuse analysis (length, character variety, duplicates)
3. Hashing and salting with hashlib and bcrypt
4. Plaintext vs hashed password comparison
5. Password validation (length, complexity, uniqueness)
6. Password policy design

## Tools
Python, bcrypt, hashlib, pandas, matplotlib, Google Colab / Jupyter Notebook

## How to run
1. Open password_security_analysis.ipynb in Google Colab or Jupyter
2. Install dependencies: pip install -r requirements.txt
3. Run all cells in order

## Key findings
- <% of weak passwords>
- <number of reused passwords>
- <how salting changed the hashes of identical passwords>
- <bcrypt vs hashlib observation, e.g. speed or cost factor>

## Password policy summary
- Minimum length: <e.g. 12 characters>
- Complexity and uniqueness rules: <...>
- Store only salted bcrypt hashes, never plaintext
- <MFA, lockout, no reuse, breach-list checks>

## Repository structure
- password_security_analysis.ipynb: main notebook
- password_policy.md: written policy
- requirements.txt: dependencies
- screenshots/: sample outputs

## Disclaimer
Educational project using synthetic data only.
